#====================================================================
# E320 draft — preserve joinable thread lifecycle without pthread_cancel
#====================================================================

id:                     E320
trigger_tool:           clang|ld|runtime
phase:                  compilation|linking|runtime
error_signature:        pthread_cancel.*undeclared|pthread_setcanceltype.*undeclared|undefined reference to pthread_cancel|undefined symbol: pthread_cancel

severity:               2
category:               libc-compat|threading|lifecycle|signal
match_keywords:         pthread_cancel, pthread_setcanceltype, JACK_DISABLE_PTHREAD_CANCEL, pthread_kill, pthread_join, SIGUSR1, joinable thread, thread exit
title:                  Preserve joinable thread teardown when pthread cancellation is unavailable

root_cause:             E085 identifies missing pthread cancellation APIs, but a no-op stub or simply returning an error changes the lifecycle of a joinable worker: callers still wait in pthread_join() and cannot reclaim the thread. A fallback must preserve both targeted exit and join semantics.
affected_scope:         Threaded C/C++ software that owns joinable worker threads and directly uses pthread_cancel()/pthread_setcanceltype(), when the target libc omits the cancellation API.
verification_cmd:       grep -R "pthread_cancel\\|pthread_setcanceltype\\|pthread_join" -n src posix common 2>/dev/null; nm -D <target-libc> | grep pthread_cancel || true

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           guarded-signal-thread-exit
rec_description:        Keep the normal pthread-cancel path when available; otherwise install a narrowly scoped async-signal-safe thread-exit handler before creating the joinable worker, send a reserved signal with pthread_kill(), and join the worker. Ensure the application's signal-mask setup does not block that reserved signal.
rec_command:            # project-specific: handler calls pthread_exit(0); fallback cancellation calls pthread_kill(thread, SIGUSR1); then pthread_join(thread, &status)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      cooperative-stop-and-join
fallback_description:   Prefer an existing project stop flag, condition-variable wakeup, or event-loop shutdown hook when the project cannot reserve a process-wide signal safely.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       int pthread_cancel\(.*\).*return 0|stub.*pthread_cancel|define.*pthread_cancel.*return 0
forbid_1_reason:        A successful-looking cancellation stub leaves the worker running and lets code incorrectly proceed to pthread_join() or resource teardown.
forbid_1_consequence:   Hangs, leaked threads, use-after-free races, or a false claim that cancellation behavior was preserved.
forbid_2_pattern:       pthread_kill\([^,]+,\s*SIGUSR1\).*without.*sigaction|sigaddset\([^,]+,\s*SIGUSR1\)
forbid_2_reason:        A signal fallback needs an installed exit handler and must remain unblocked in the target worker context.
forbid_2_consequence:   The worker does not exit and pthread_join() blocks indefinitely.

principles:             P004, P015
causes:                 []
caused_by:              [E085, E127]
similar_to:             [E022]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E320-draft-ASP1-pthread-cancel-lifecycle.md
last_updated:           2026-08-12
source_event:           JACK 1.9.22 PR #3482 pthread cancellation fallback
authors:                ASP1R1N <sukurajimayilei@gmail.com>
